00:15:09.883 --> 00:15:12.469
And a clear TiVo equals a clear mind.

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:16.639
Are we okay with the kids going
to that concert?

00:15:16.847 --> 00:15:19.516
- Yeah.
- What if Rooney is, like...

00:15:19.683 --> 00:15:23.186
...death-metal Satan-worshipping
speed freaks?

00:15:23.394 --> 00:15:26.230
Honey, that went out in the late '90s.

00:15:27.273 --> 00:15:29.441
I saw it on a special on E!

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:33.528
I'll run Rooney up my proverbial flagpole,
but you have got to speak to Hailey.

00:15:37.615 --> 00:15:38.907
So?

00:15:39.116 --> 00:15:44.662
- Yeah, it's my first time hearing it, so...
- That's why we're doing a run-through.

00:15:44.871 --> 00:15:47.706
- So you'll have heard it all before tonight.
- Right.

00:15:47.915 --> 00:15:50.292
- So we're going tonight?
- No. It's your first concert.

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:53.837
We have free tickets, backstage passes.
You're right, we should skip it.

00:15:54.045 --> 00:15:57.548
- That's not what I'm saying.
- What are you saying?

00:15:58.716 --> 00:16:01.968
- Have you met Natalie?
- No, but I hear she's great.

00:16:02.177 --> 00:16:05.721
- And Oliver is...? I mean...
- Is someone jealous?

00:16:07.723 --> 00:16:12.894
This song is good.
Turn it up. Really, really loud.

00:16:21.026 --> 00:16:26.072
Oliver will be with Natalie.
Rooney is a really good band.

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:29.283
- And tonight we're gonna have fun.
- I know.

00:16:29.491 --> 00:16:33.661
- There won't be dancing, right?
- I'll dance. You can watch.

00:16:33.828 --> 00:16:35.913
Works for me.

00:16:47.506 --> 00:16:49.049
- I think that's enough.
- What?

00:16:49.258 --> 00:16:51.760
There was almost a knee bend.
You were about to find the beat.

00:16:51.968 --> 00:16:55.054
- And?
- Remember cousin Jeffery's bar mitzvah?

00:16:55.221 --> 00:16:57.681
You almost wiped out a dozen kids
on the dance floor.

00:16:57.890 --> 00:17:00.475
That "Y.M.C.A." song
requires a lot of movement.

00:17:00.684 --> 00:17:04.812
- I'm just trying to spare casualties.
- So anyone gonna be doing drugs?

00:17:05.021 --> 00:17:07.148
I hope so, otherwise
it's a lame-ass concert.

00:17:07.356 --> 00:17:09.274
Anyone named Seth
gonna be doing any drugs?

00:17:09.483 --> 00:17:12.027
No. Nobody named Seth Cohen.
I promise.

00:17:12.235 --> 00:17:14.529
Gotta stay sharp.
It's my first date with Anna.

00:17:14.737 --> 00:17:17.948
It is? So you and Summer
finally had the talk?

00:17:18.157 --> 00:17:20.158
Oh, yes, almost several times.

00:17:20.367 --> 00:17:21.910
- Seth.
- Father.

00:17:22.118 --> 00:17:25.079
The sooner you tell her,
the better you'll feel about everything.

00:17:25.288 --> 00:17:27.081
See, I don't really believe that.

00:17:27.289 --> 00:17:31.835
I'm feeling like the longer I wait
to tell her, the longer I'll feel great.

00:17:32.043 --> 00:17:34.003
The best advice
I can give you is this.

00:17:34.212 --> 00:17:37.131
It's from Steven Seagal in
his classic film Hard to Kill.

00:17:38.132 --> 00:17:41.718
"The anticipation of death
is far worse than death itself."

00:17:41.927 --> 00:17:44.929
Great. So then we both agree
that Summer's gonna kill me.

00:17:45.138 --> 00:17:47.890
Look, if you're old enough
to go to a concert alone...

00:17:48.057 --> 00:17:50.892
...if you're old enough to embark
on a real relationship...

00:17:51.101 --> 00:17:53.520
...you are old enough to be a man.

00:17:55.354 --> 00:17:59.066
Well, she's not gonna be
there tonight...

00:17:59.274 --> 00:18:01.109
...so I'll tell her Monday.
- Good.

00:18:01.985 --> 00:18:05.196
Now, get going. Your mother
and I want some time alone.

00:18:05.655 --> 00:18:08.490
There's a visual that
I don't want to take with me tonight.

00:18:08.657 --> 00:18:11.535
Well, son, your mom's a hottie,
and I got her.

00:18:18.707 --> 00:18:22.168
- I don't see him.
- Maybe he's inside.

00:18:24.212 --> 00:18:27.256
- Excuse me, are you on the list?
- Yeah, we're with Oliver Trask.

00:18:27.465 --> 00:18:29.758
- Who's Oliver Trask?
- You don't have his name?

00:18:29.967 --> 00:18:34.470
No, I don't have his name.
I've never heard it. That's why I'm asking.

00:18:34.679 --> 00:18:38.766
- Thanks, you've been very helpful.
- I'll call him and see where he is.

00:18:38.974 --> 00:18:41.309
- A lot of freaks here, huh, Cohen?
- Yeah.

00:18:41.518 --> 00:18:44.812
Good job, Luke. That should
help make us a lot of friends.

00:18:45.021 --> 00:18:46.480
- Damn it.
- What?

00:18:46.689 --> 00:18:50.817
Well, dude, they're gonna go on soon.
If Oliver's late, we'll miss the first song.

00:18:51.026 --> 00:18:55.154
They only have one album. Factor in
your standard cover, that's 12 songs.

00:18:55.321 --> 00:18:57.740
Oh, no. But, hey. I mean, come on.

00:18:57.948 --> 00:19:01.034
If we don't get in,
we're still gonna have fun tonight.

00:19:01.243 --> 00:19:02.952
- Right?
- What are we gonna do?

00:19:03.536 --> 00:19:06.289
I hope you guys aren't waiting for me.

00:19:07.581 --> 00:19:09.541
- Summer.
- Cohen.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.419
- Hey, Anna.
- Summer.

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:17.339
- Who are you talking to?
- It just goes straight to voice mail.

00:19:17.506 --> 00:19:20.008
Dude, look at that freak.

00:19:20.217 --> 00:19:22.093
Hey, I drove alone.
Will you ride with me?

00:19:22.302 --> 00:19:25.430
You want to give up so early?
Maybe I can grease a few palms.

00:19:25.638 --> 00:19:27.431
Hey.

00:19:28.432 --> 00:19:30.434
- There you are.
- What's up, man?

00:19:30.642 --> 00:19:33.394
- Hi.
- I thought you were a no-show.

00:19:33.603 --> 00:19:36.897
- What happened? I said back door.
- No, you didn't.

00:19:37.106 --> 00:19:40.442
- Load in here, guys.
- The band's here.

00:19:40.651 --> 00:19:42.110
- It's all happening.
- What up, guys?

00:19:42.319 --> 00:19:45.238
Robert, how's it going?
Good to see you.

00:19:45.446 --> 00:19:46.906
Looking forward to the show.

00:19:47.073 --> 00:19:49.908
- Thank you.
- I guess we're on time.

00:19:50.117 --> 00:19:52.786
- Which one's Rooney?
- They're all Rooney.

00:19:52.952 --> 00:19:56.622
- Hey, man, this is my posse.
- This is crazy.

00:19:57.415 --> 00:20:01.960
- Hey. So where's Natalie?
- Yeah, we had another fight.

00:20:02.168 --> 00:20:06.464
This whole long-distance thing's tough.
Looks like I'm dateless tonight.

00:20:06.672 --> 00:20:09.758
Hey, no! No way.
We'll be your date, right?

00:20:10.467 --> 00:20:11.760
Yeah, right.

00:20:11.968 --> 00:20:16.639
- So should we fire up the hot tub?
- Interesting. Open a bottle of wine.

00:20:16.847 --> 00:20:18.974
Oh, I like it.

00:20:19.183 --> 00:20:21.268
First, TiVo. I'm gonna
erase Hailey's programs.

00:20:21.476 --> 00:20:23.019
- Hot pizza?
- Hailey.

00:20:23.186 --> 00:20:25.521
Hey, guys. You're just in time.

00:20:26.480 --> 00:20:28.857
Doctor. Doctor.

00:20:29.691 --> 00:20:32.444
- James.
- What's up?

00:20:33.695 --> 00:20:36.113
I just thought that you were
going out tonight.

00:20:36.322 --> 00:20:40.200
We were. But then I found out there's
a Golden Girls marathon on Lifetime.

00:20:40.409 --> 00:20:42.869
And I decided to dig up
all my favorite board games.

00:20:43.078 --> 00:20:45.746
We're having a throwback
to the old babysitting days.

00:20:45.913 --> 00:20:50.292
- Why don't you guys join us?
- Great. That would be great.

00:20:51.168 --> 00:20:54.712
Oh, I love this episode. This is the one
where Rose adopts the pig.

00:20:54.921 --> 00:20:56.380
She adopted the pig?

00:21:05.763 --> 00:21:08.515
- Do you play?
- A little.

00:21:08.682 --> 00:21:11.018
- Here, man.
- All access? Sweet.

00:21:12.519 --> 00:21:15.188
- Hey, it's cool?
- It's cool.

00:21:15.354 --> 00:21:17.189
- Hey, check it out.
- Seriously?

00:21:17.398 --> 00:21:19.233
Yeah.

00:21:19.441 --> 00:21:24.195
Awesome.
I just got a few songs that I wrote.

00:21:33.328 --> 00:21:36.330
Okay, I'm just gonna...

00:21:37.123 --> 00:21:39.541
Seth, you have to tell her tonight.

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:42.252
- No, I don't.
- Hey.

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:43.837
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

00:21:44.045 --> 00:21:46.422
- So, Luke, he's...
- Yeah, we don't let him out much.

00:21:50.717 --> 00:21:53.011
Yeah. But you guys are cool,
having fun?

00:21:53.219 --> 00:21:55.179
- Everything's awesome.
- Glad to hear it.

00:21:55.388 --> 00:21:57.765
Yeah. Everything is not awesome.

00:21:57.973 --> 00:22:00.976
If I don't tell Summer tonight,
then later, when I do tell her...

00:22:01.184 --> 00:22:04.270
...she'll remember the fun she had
at Rooney. That will cheer her up.

00:22:04.479 --> 00:22:08.899
There's never gonna be a good time
to tell her. Tonight's not a bad night.

00:22:09.108 --> 00:22:13.862
There's a lot of guys here.
Cute guys, older guys. A lot of musicians.

00:22:14.070 --> 00:22:16.280
Girls like musicians.

00:22:16.489 --> 00:22:18.782
Maybe you're right.

00:22:19.491 --> 00:22:22.577
Am I flattering myself
to even think that Summer'll care?

00:22:22.786 --> 00:22:27.456
I mean, me compared
to that dude or that guy.

00:22:27.665 --> 00:22:29.541
- Right.
- Are you checking out dudes again?

00:22:30.167 --> 00:22:31.751
No.

00:22:31.960 --> 00:22:35.630
But there are plenty here tonight,
aren't there? A lot of musicians.

00:22:35.838 --> 00:22:38.299
In fact, I think I'm gonna go
find some myself.

00:22:38.507 --> 00:22:42.552
Why don't you and Seth talk.
You know, about anything.

00:22:43.803 --> 00:22:48.599
- Cohen, you and Anna...?
- Me and Anna what? What?

00:22:49.933 --> 00:22:52.102
Will you guys stand with me
at the concert?

00:22:52.310 --> 00:22:54.979
Marissa's on a date,
and I'm all alone tonight, so...

00:22:55.146 --> 00:22:56.439
Okay, that would be nice.

00:23:05.780 --> 00:23:10.158
Yeah. Hey, man. I thought your boy
was supposed to be here an hour ago.

00:23:10.367 --> 00:23:12.327
No. Okay, no excuses.

00:23:12.535 --> 00:23:17.456
I don't care who you send. Just make
sure it's good and it gets here quick.

00:23:17.665 --> 00:23:19.458
All right.

00:23:31.093 --> 00:23:35.221
I can't see. I'm stuck behind
a row of giants. Come with me.

00:23:35.388 --> 00:23:36.847
Okay, lead the way.

00:23:41.476 --> 00:23:43.728
Sorry.

00:23:46.647 --> 00:23:49.650
Hey. Did you tell her?
What did she say? Did she leave?

00:23:49.817 --> 00:23:52.110
No. Summer is bringing refreshments
for her friends.

00:23:52.319 --> 00:23:56.364
- Seth said you were thirsty.
- Yeah. You are thirsty, aren't you?

00:23:58.407 --> 00:23:59.950
- You suck.
- I'm sorry.

00:24:01.243 --> 00:24:05.121
- I gotta pee. You gotta pee?
- I'll come with you.

00:24:05.538 --> 00:24:06.747
I'm telling her.

00:24:12.877 --> 00:24:16.797
You know the night that Mom and Dad
came home early from Palm Springs?

00:24:17.006 --> 00:24:19.174
And we flushed all that beer
down the toilet.

00:24:19.383 --> 00:24:21.009
- A lot of good that did.
- I know.

00:24:21.218 --> 00:24:23.261
Dad caught you
throwing out the empty bottles.

00:24:23.720 --> 00:24:25.972
- I thought you were sleeping.
- Face it, sister.

00:24:26.180 --> 00:24:27.890
Everything I know,
I learned from you.

00:24:28.098 --> 00:24:29.892
You were a bad influence
back in the day.

00:24:30.100 --> 00:24:32.269
How do you think I learned
to piss off Dad?

00:24:32.477 --> 00:24:36.188
- The student becomes the master.
- And the master becomes Dad's slave.

00:24:36.397 --> 00:24:41.068
Helping to turn paradise into a parking lot,
or at least a three-car garage.

00:24:44.028 --> 00:24:46.447
Hey, Connect Four!

00:24:46.656 --> 00:24:49.074
Congratulations.
Next Saturday, Yahtzee.

00:24:49.283 --> 00:24:52.160
No, wait. Stay. Battleship? Uno?

00:24:52.327 --> 00:24:54.287
You know, Sandy's right. It's late.

00:24:54.495 --> 00:24:57.832
And, besides, I have a show home
waiting for me in the morning.

00:24:58.040 --> 00:25:00.792
Just what Orange County needs.
Another show home.

00:25:00.959 --> 00:25:04.212
Airlifted from the McMansion factory
and dropped from the sky...

00:25:04.420 --> 00:25:07.089
The one on the bluff,
that's a great house.

00:25:07.256 --> 00:25:11.843
If by "great" you mean overbuilt,
overpriced and exactly like this one.

00:25:12.052 --> 00:25:15.263
- Oh, nice. Hailey, nice.
- I was kidding.

00:25:15.471 --> 00:25:18.807
- I'm laughing on the inside.
- I'm not. You're living in our home.

00:25:19.016 --> 00:25:23.478
You're insulting my wife.
You're driving my whole family crazy.

00:25:23.645 --> 00:25:25.521
- Is this true?
- Yeah.

00:25:25.730 --> 00:25:27.815
And we all know
what you're doing here.

00:25:30.192 --> 00:25:32.986
She didn't mean anything.
It's just sisters.

00:25:33.153 --> 00:25:36.239
No, all this talk about plans,
about growing up, it's shtick.

00:25:36.405 --> 00:25:39.241
It's a routine. And it's tired.

00:25:39.408 --> 00:25:41.576
You know who's tired? Me.
So why don't we stop.

00:25:41.785 --> 00:25:43.078
No, stop protecting her.

00:25:43.578 --> 00:25:46.956
You're not even nice to Kirsten.
She's the only reason we put up with you.

00:25:47.164 --> 00:25:51.626
Well, you won't have to put up with me
for much longer, okay?

00:26:00.217 --> 00:26:02.302
- Sorry?
- It's not your fault, Jimmy.

00:26:02.510 --> 00:26:04.470
No, I meant the board game.

00:26:20.609 --> 00:26:22.402
- You like The Golden Girls?
- Yes.

00:26:22.611 --> 00:26:25.613
There's a marathon on.
I can't get the song out of my head.

00:26:25.780 --> 00:26:27.406
I love The Golden Girls.

00:26:27.573 --> 00:26:29.783
It's not Rose's fault.
She just is that way.

00:26:29.992 --> 00:26:32.077
You're Rose? I'm Blanche.

00:26:32.285 --> 00:26:35.288
It's kind of weird that I relate
to a 70-year-old, but...

00:26:35.455 --> 00:26:38.040
How good was the episode
when there was a blackout?

00:26:38.249 --> 00:26:40.375
How about when Rose adopts the pig?

00:26:40.584 --> 00:26:44.712
Then Sophia loses her glasses
and thinks the pig is a baby.

00:26:44.921 --> 00:26:46.756
It's so funny.

00:26:57.848 --> 00:27:00.601
Jimmy, wait.

00:27:00.851 --> 00:27:04.896
Sorry about that in there.
My little tantrum.

00:27:05.104 --> 00:27:10.692
Oh, listen, it's complicated between
you and your sister. It always has been.

00:27:10.859 --> 00:27:12.944
You gotta go, like, right now?

00:27:13.153 --> 00:27:17.198
Yeah, I don't know if I ever told you,
but I'm an extremely important person.

00:27:17.364 --> 00:27:20.242
And so I have to...

00:27:20.701 --> 00:27:24.245
Yeah. No, Marissa's at a concert.

00:27:25.496 --> 00:27:27.706
Yep, nothing but time.

00:27:28.499 --> 00:27:30.584
Didn't tonight feel like
the good old days?

00:27:31.543 --> 00:27:37.548
No. It was more like two kind of pathetic
people grasping for the old days.

00:27:37.840 --> 00:27:41.426
- Right. That too.
- Yeah.

00:27:41.635 --> 00:27:45.013
Look, the good old days.
They're exactly that.

00:27:45.221 --> 00:27:48.849
Would you really want to be back
in high school?

00:27:50.309 --> 00:27:51.935
- Yeah.
- Yeah. I would too.

00:27:52.686 --> 00:27:58.982
- And you think I'm pathetic?
- Yes, I do. It's sad, really.

00:28:14.996 --> 00:28:17.331
I always had a crush on you.
You know that?

00:28:17.832 --> 00:28:21.751
No. You were 8
when I went away to college.

00:28:21.960 --> 00:28:24.254
So I wasn't...

00:28:29.049 --> 00:28:32.761
You're Kirsten's sister.

00:28:33.636 --> 00:28:35.430
So I've heard all my life.

00:28:36.013 --> 00:28:38.682
Look, we don't want to make
a complicated situation...

00:28:38.891 --> 00:28:40.892
...even more complicated, right?

00:28:41.309 --> 00:28:46.355
The last thing we need is having
Sandy or Kirsten catching us.

00:28:46.564 --> 00:28:49.483
Unless that's what you're hoping for.

00:28:51.860 --> 00:28:55.196
Look, your sister is amazing...

00:28:55.405 --> 00:28:58.699
...and Sandy is such a great guy.

00:28:58.907 --> 00:29:02.035
I think you're lucky
to have them looking out for you.

00:29:02.994 --> 00:29:05.163
I know that I am.

00:29:09.041 --> 00:29:10.834
I'm gonna go.

00:29:11.043 --> 00:29:12.961
Okay.

00:30:41.034 --> 00:30:43.703
- Hi. I'm gonna...
- Hey, this is great, right?

00:30:43.870 --> 00:30:45.663
Perfect.

00:30:46.789 --> 00:30:49.291
Come here a second.

00:31:10.475 --> 00:31:12.519
- What are we doing?
- This is better.

00:31:12.727 --> 00:31:15.897
Wait. But we're missing the concert.
We can't ditch Oliver.

00:31:16.105 --> 00:31:19.817
- Oliver's fine. He's friends with the band.
- And with us.

00:31:20.025 --> 00:31:22.777
I thought you said you wanted us
to hang out with friends.

00:31:22.944 --> 00:31:26.280
You've known him two weeks.
How good a friend can he be?

00:31:26.489 --> 00:31:29.074
Look. He's in recovery,
trying to stay clean.

00:31:29.283 --> 00:31:30.826
We can talk about stuff.

00:31:31.034 --> 00:31:33.453
He tells me things.
What he's going through.

00:31:33.661 --> 00:31:36.330
- Unlike me, right?
- I didn't say that.

00:31:40.876 --> 00:31:42.961
I know you didn't want
to come here tonight...

00:31:43.169 --> 00:31:45.463
...so, I mean,
I guess if you want to leave...

00:31:46.922 --> 00:31:48.424
Right.

00:31:49.299 --> 00:31:50.926
Later.

00:32:01.643 --> 00:32:03.645
Hey, Luke.

00:32:03.853 --> 00:32:06.772
- You know who sings this song?
- Rooney.

00:32:07.606 --> 00:32:10.359
- Rooney!
- We should keep it that way.

00:32:10.525 --> 00:32:12.652
Yeah, Rooney!

00:32:24.412 --> 00:32:26.247
What the hell, man?! Get off me!

00:32:29.249 --> 00:32:32.752
- Hey, get off him!
- I'm a cop.

00:32:33.586 --> 00:32:36.756
- What? There's gotta be some mistake.
- Yeah. His.

00:32:36.964 --> 00:32:39.466
He just tried to buy
3 grams of coke from me.

00:32:41.051 --> 00:32:44.053
Ryan, go back inside.
Don't tell anybody.

00:33:24.921 --> 00:33:28.882
Excuse me, barkeep, sir.

00:33:29.883 --> 00:33:32.302
- Hey.
- What can I get you?

00:33:32.927 --> 00:33:36.681
How did you do that? The usual.

00:33:36.931 --> 00:33:38.390
- Mountain Dew.
- How many?

00:33:39.725 --> 00:33:41.726
Unfortunately, three.

00:33:41.935 --> 00:33:44.145
So Anna's telling Summer
that we're a couple.

00:33:44.354 --> 00:33:47.731
When they get back, I will officially
be in a relationship with Anna.

00:33:47.940 --> 00:33:50.609
Unless Summer kills me,
in which case, you've been like a brother.

00:33:50.817 --> 00:33:52.611
Good, because I need
your keys and phone.

00:33:52.777 --> 00:33:55.780
- Yeah, you okay?
- I'm fine. It's Oliver.

00:33:56.239 --> 00:33:59.575
- What? What's going on?
- Tell you later?

00:33:59.783 --> 00:34:01.993
All right. You'll miss
a hell of a show, though.

00:34:02.202 --> 00:34:04.412
Rooney's not bad, either.

00:34:07.665 --> 00:34:11.043
- Is Jimmy gone?
- Yeah. Is she all right?

00:34:11.251 --> 00:34:13.545
I knocked. She didn't answer.

00:34:13.753 --> 00:34:15.546
Maybe she's giving us the house back.

00:34:15.755 --> 00:34:19.883
Or maybe she's packing and she'll
be gone in the morning. And frankly...

00:34:20.092 --> 00:34:24.137
...I'd rather have her here, where I can
keep an eye on her, than anywhere else.

00:34:24.345 --> 00:34:29.558
You can't keep her here forever. It's no
good for her and it's no good for us.

00:34:30.392 --> 00:34:31.768
Hello?

00:34:32.936 --> 00:34:35.063
Hey, what's wrong?

00:34:35.354 --> 00:34:37.690
Where are you?

00:34:38.357 --> 00:34:39.900
I'll be right there.

00:34:40.067 --> 00:34:42.736
Ryan's at the police station.

00:34:50.826 --> 00:34:53.745
Thank you, Newport Beach.
Good night, everybody.

00:35:01.751 --> 00:35:03.586
- Seth.
- Hey.

00:35:03.795 --> 00:35:05.963
- Where have you been?
- At the bar. How was it?

00:35:06.172 --> 00:35:08.382
It was amazing.
They played the whole album.

00:35:08.590 --> 00:35:11.593
Not with Rooney, how did it go
with Summer? Did you tell her?

00:35:11.760 --> 00:35:13.928
Tell me what?

00:35:20.642 --> 00:35:21.935
So you're a couple?

00:35:22.143 --> 00:35:23.686
- No.
- Yes.

00:35:23.895 --> 00:35:28.274
We wanted to tell you first before we
became a couple, which now we are.

00:35:28.440 --> 00:35:30.400
- So you chose Anna?
- No.

00:35:30.692 --> 00:35:34.028
Kind of, yeah.
She came over on New Year's Eve.

00:35:34.237 --> 00:35:36.155
You were with me on New Year's Eve.

00:35:36.364 --> 00:35:39.616
Technically, you were with
that guy Allan, remember?

00:35:39.825 --> 00:35:44.370
And you kept insisting that
I go find someone to kiss, so I did.

00:35:44.579 --> 00:35:48.249
I was taking out the garbage, she was
in the driveway. You know how it goes.

00:35:48.457 --> 00:35:51.209
Okay, well, congrats.

00:35:53.253 --> 00:35:55.379
You're not mad?

00:35:58.007 --> 00:36:01.259
Good, because I didn't want this
to affect our relationship in any way.

00:36:01.468 --> 00:36:04.220
Well, Anna, I have to say...

00:36:04.387 --> 00:36:08.349
...that Rose would've never pulled
that New Year's stunt on Blanche.

00:36:08.557 --> 00:36:10.392
I know. I'm sorry.

00:36:10.601 --> 00:36:13.937
Although Blanche
would've done it to Rose, so...

00:36:15.104 --> 00:36:18.357
So can we still all hang out?
Will you be cool with that?

00:36:18.565 --> 00:36:21.568
We'd both really like that
if we could hang out.

00:36:23.236 --> 00:36:27.198
Sure. You guys,
we can totally hang out.

00:36:27.406 --> 00:36:30.617
I mean, in fact,
what are you guys doing right now?

00:36:40.500 --> 00:36:43.253
So they're gonna let him go.

00:36:43.420 --> 00:36:46.339
- Really? How'd you do that?
- I'm just that good.

00:36:46.505 --> 00:36:50.217
- I used to play poker with these guys.
- Thanks for doing this.

00:36:50.425 --> 00:36:53.178
- You didn't have to, really.
- Is this kid a friend of yours?

00:36:53.386 --> 00:36:54.846
He's a friend of Marissa's.

00:36:55.054 --> 00:36:57.890
They met in therapy.
He said he's been clean a while, but...

00:36:58.057 --> 00:36:59.600
They busted him trying to buy coke.

00:36:59.808 --> 00:37:03.144
Then he said his parents are away
for a month. Can you believe that?

00:37:03.353 --> 00:37:05.146
A parent leaves a kid
like that on his own.

00:37:05.313 --> 00:37:07.023
Yeah, imagine that.

00:37:08.440 --> 00:37:10.859
- I'll never understand it.
- I hope not.

00:37:12.736 --> 00:37:16.072
- I'm glad you called me.
- Me too.

00:37:23.119 --> 00:37:27.164
I'm gonna finish up your paperwork.
You sit tight. I'll be right back.

00:37:33.169 --> 00:37:36.172
So thanks.

00:37:36.922 --> 00:37:39.216
Seth's dad seems cool.

00:37:40.259 --> 00:37:42.302
He is.

00:37:43.845 --> 00:37:46.514
So why'd you do this for me?

00:37:47.098 --> 00:37:49.683
I mean, you don't even like me, man.

00:37:50.517 --> 00:37:52.644
I don't really know you.

00:37:53.770 --> 00:37:59.650
Well, if it's any consolation, I don't
like myself very much right now, either.

00:38:04.904 --> 00:38:08.782
- So, what happened?
- I don't know.

00:38:08.991 --> 00:38:13.828
Natalie didn't show.
And then I saw you and Marissa.

00:38:14.495 --> 00:38:16.664
Your friends.

00:38:17.665 --> 00:38:19.291
Then it hit me.

00:38:19.458 --> 00:38:23.420
I have no one. My parents are gone.

00:38:23.628 --> 00:38:28.173
My friends,
if you can even call them that...

00:38:28.382 --> 00:38:31.134
...they all disappeared
when I got clean.

00:38:31.301 --> 00:38:33.261
Now I...

00:38:38.849 --> 00:38:42.894
There's Marissa.
Seth likes your taste in music.

00:38:43.770 --> 00:38:46.314
And Luke pretty much
likes everybody at this point.

00:38:49.149 --> 00:38:53.695
And what about you? I mean, you must
like me a little to get me out of jail.

00:38:53.903 --> 00:38:56.656
No, that was Sandy.

00:39:06.163 --> 00:39:08.040
Marissa.

00:39:08.707 --> 00:39:10.417
You gonna tell her?

00:39:11.001 --> 00:39:12.877
No.

00:39:13.378 --> 00:39:15.088
You are.

00:39:23.136 --> 00:39:25.013
Hey.

00:39:25.471 --> 00:39:27.556
Yeah, it's Oliver.

00:39:42.861 --> 00:39:45.279
Hey, whoa, hey, hey, hey!

00:39:45.488 --> 00:39:48.073
- I can't have half?
- There are other bagels.

00:39:48.282 --> 00:39:52.160
- Not salt bagels.
- You ate them all. And several sesame.

00:39:53.578 --> 00:39:56.330
I haven't been the best guest, I know.

00:39:57.123 --> 00:40:01.877
- And what you said tonight...
- Hey, Connect Four was happening.

00:40:02.085 --> 00:40:04.379
It gets my blood up.

00:40:04.587 --> 00:40:06.756
Well, you were right.

00:40:09.675 --> 00:40:15.179
So, what's the plan? Hit Caleb up
for more cash. And then what?

00:40:15.346 --> 00:40:19.975
- Europe this time? Iceland? Boca?
- I don't know.

00:40:20.976 --> 00:40:25.271
You know, I see how happy you guys are,
and I think, "Why can't I have that?"

00:40:25.480 --> 00:40:27.857
- Because you don't want it.
- How do you know?

00:40:28.065 --> 00:40:30.651
I don't even know what I want.

00:40:31.985 --> 00:40:34.028
You could stay here.

00:40:34.237 --> 00:40:36.656
I mean, not here exactly...

00:40:36.947 --> 00:40:39.324
...but, you know, get a home.

00:40:41.243 --> 00:40:45.621
- A job. Settle down.
- No.

00:40:46.831 --> 00:40:50.751
See, that's the thing.
All I know is what I don't want.

00:40:50.959 --> 00:40:55.171
Well, that's not entirely true.

00:40:58.632 --> 00:41:00.592
And the rest...

00:41:01.009 --> 00:41:04.137
...you'll figure out. Good night.

00:41:04.679 --> 00:41:06.472
Good night.

00:41:17.023 --> 00:41:19.149
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:41:19.900 --> 00:41:21.860
No, wait, don't get up.

00:41:30.659 --> 00:41:32.327
Thanks.

00:41:33.912 --> 00:41:35.621
He's not a bad guy, Oliver. He's...

00:41:35.830 --> 00:41:37.206
This may come as a shock to you...

00:41:37.415 --> 00:41:40.751
...but right now,
I don't want to talk about Oliver.

00:41:48.549 --> 00:41:51.384
Oh, hey, wow, kissing.
Sorry about that.

00:41:51.593 --> 00:41:54.971
We're gonna hang out inside, but
you guys are obviously alone together...

00:41:55.179 --> 00:41:56.222
...so do that.

00:41:56.430 --> 00:41:59.516
- Ryan, what happened to you?
- Luke, please, you're shouting.

00:41:59.683 --> 00:42:03.978
- Someone stood too close to the speaker.
- Dude, that concert did not suck at all.

00:42:04.187 --> 00:42:09.149
- We PlayStationing it, or what?
- Yeah. Any time you want to join us.

00:42:09.358 --> 00:42:11.693
Let's go before he wakes up
your parents.

00:42:11.902 --> 00:42:13.570
Think we can teach him to fetch?

00:42:13.778 --> 00:42:17.990
I don't want to be the third wheel
or watch you guys make out, so enjoy.

00:42:19.867 --> 00:42:23.995
- Well, we could stay here.
- Yeah, but maybe we should...

00:42:24.746 --> 00:42:26.622
Race you?

00:42:27.456 --> 00:42:29.666
Cohen, you've played
this game before?

00:42:29.875 --> 00:42:32.544
See the way I ripped
that guy's spine out?

00:42:32.711 --> 00:42:34.837
Sitting right here, buddy.

00:42:36.922 --> 00:42:41.802
I am so glad we all could hang out
together like this, aren't you guys?

00:42:43.178 --> 00:42:44.387
- Yeah.
- Damn it.

00:42:44.595 --> 00:42:46.138
- Ryan, you're up.
- You're up, Ryan.

00:42:46.347 --> 00:42:48.766
We'll make it best of five.
